---
import { version } from "../../../../npm/magistr/package.json";
import recording from "../../public/demo/tic-tac-toe/recording.json";
import { minutes, walkthroughEnd } from "../data/build-recording.mjs";
import { siteName, tagline, definition, description } from "../data/brand.mjs";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import BuildWalkthrough from "../components/BuildWalkthrough.astro";
import {highlightCode} from "../../scripts/highlight-recording.mjs";
const installCode = await highlightCode("npm install --global magistr@beta\nmagistr --version","shellscript");
const buildMinutes = minutes(recording, walkthroughEnd(recording));
const jsonLd = [
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebSite","name":"Magistr","url":"https://magistr.dev",description},
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Magistr","applicationCategory":"DeveloperApplication","operatingSystem":"macOS (Apple Silicon)","softwareVersion":version,description,"url":"https://magistr.dev","downloadUrl":"https://magistr.dev/docs/installation","softwareRequirements":"macOS 15 or later, Rust 1.95 or later, Git"}
];
---
<Base title={siteName + " · " + tagline} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero section-shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <h1 id="hero-title">{tagline}</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">{definition}</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="#workflow">Follow a real build <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        <a id="install-btn" class="button button-quiet" href="#install">Install Magistr</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">Works with Codex and Claude Code. Other agents connect through MCP.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="workflow" class="section-shell section-block example-section" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="workflow-title">A real build, start to finish.</h2>
        <p>Codex built a complete tic-tac-toe game in Bevy 0.20.0 with Magistr in {buildMinutes} minutes. Follow the session, open the roadmap at any moment, and see why the opponent looks ahead.</p>
      </div>
      <BuildWalkthrough />
      <aside class="builder-note" aria-labelledby="builder-title">
        <h3 id="builder-title">Why I’m building this</h3>
        <p>I want to work through a big idea with an agent and still know where we are when I come back tomorrow. That’s why I’m building Magistr.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="product" class="section-shell section-block project-followthrough" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="product-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="product-title">The next session has somewhere to start.</h2>
        <p>The agent can read the plan, find the opponent experiment, and see which checks passed. You can spend the next conversation on what you want to build next.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="project-capabilities">
        <div><dt><a href="/docs/roadmap">Plan the bigger project</a></dt><dd>Keep deliverables, dependencies and acceptance criteria together. Change the plan as you learn more.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><a href="/docs/reasoning">Remember why</a></dt><dd>Save an investigation and the evidence behind its conclusion. Revisit it when the assumptions change.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><a href="/docs/chunks">Finish a piece</a></dt><dd>Give the agent one chunk or a bounded run. Keep the task, changes and checks attached to the work.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><a href="/docs/feedback">Save feedback</a></dt><dd>Want an easier opponent? Keep that idea, investigate the options, then decide whether it belongs on the roadmap.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><a href="/docs/concepts#source-tools">Work in the code</a></dt><dd>Find and read source, check that a file is still current before editing it, and undo changes recorded in the journal.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section id="agents" class="section-shell section-block agent-section" aria-labelledby="agents-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="agents-title">Keep the agent you like.</h2>
        <p>Codex and Claude Code have setup and project workflows ready to use. Other agents can connect through MCP. Your model account and permissions stay with your agent.</p>
        <a class="text-link section-link" href="/docs/agents">Connect your agent ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="install" class="section-shell section-block install-section" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="install-title">
      <div class="install-grid">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="install-title">Install the beta</h2>
          <p>v{version} is a beta pre-release on npm, with the prebuilt executable included. You can also build it from the <a href="https://github.com/AlrikOlson/magistr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">public source repository<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</p>
          <p>You'll need Apple Silicon macOS 15 or later and Node.js with npm. Bring your own Codex or Claude Code account.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/installation">Full installation instructions</a>
        </div>
        <div class="code-panel">
          <div class="code-label"><span>In your terminal</span><button class="copy-button" type="button" aria-label="Copy commands" data-copy="source-install" hidden>Copy commands</button></div>
          <div id="source-install" set:html={installCode} />
          <p class="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="install-next">Run <code>magistr init .</code> in the project you want to build. Setup connects your agent and helps you choose the project’s checks. Setup does not start implementation. Open a session, talk through the project, and use <code>magistr next</code> when you’re ready for the first chunk.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
<script is:inline>
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-copy]").forEach((button) => {
    button.hidden = false;
    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const source = document.getElementById(button.dataset.copy);
      const status = button.closest(".code-panel")?.querySelector(".copy-status");
      if (!source || !status) return;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(source.textContent);
        status.textContent = "Commands copied.";
      } catch {
        status.textContent = "Copy is unavailable. Select the commands above to copy them.";
      }
    });
  });
</script>
